ezprestapiprovider (deprecated)
===============================

REST API v1 and v2 are served by one extension, ezprestapi (https://github.com/se7enxweb/ezprestapi).
Since 6.0.4 this extension is a compatibility shim and adds nothing of its own:

- ezpRestApiProvider extends ezp7xRestApiProvider and ezpRestContentController extends
  ezp7xRestContentController, so a rest.ini or code that names the old classes keeps working;
- its rest.ini maps the prefixes ezp and ezpl to ezp7xRestApiProvider, the same values ezprestapi sets,
  so activating both, in either order, gives the same API;
- the classes it used to share with ezprestapi (ezpRestAtomController, ezpRestAtomView, ezpRestAtomDecorator,
  ezpRestContentModel, ezpRestApiViewController) are only in ezprestapi now.

The v1 URLs (/api/ezp/v1/content/node/<id>/list/offset/0/limit/20?ResponseGroups=Fields and the rest)
answer with the same bodies as before. Migrate by activating ezprestapi and removing
ActiveExtensions[]=ezprestapiprovider, then clear the INI cache and regenerate the extension autoloads.
